  "evidence_root": "build/swat/review/room-search/",
  "scope": "One assigned officer physically searches supported room coverage, acts only on observed occupants/weapons, clears a leaf or cuffed aisle occupant through ordinary interactions, resumes after interruption and reports route completion. The full vertical-slice goal remains active.",
  "changes": [
    "Search room selects a visible room surface or door and captures its room identity through radio delay and queued Execute, assigning one eligible officer while others retain their tasks.",
    "Nine supported coverage regions with eight bounded views each; visible people/weapons use ordinary restraint/retrieval. Opaque cover hides targets, visual threats and received gunshots pause search, and Hold/human takeover cancel it.",
    "Routes stay on the room floor. Stale open-leaf routes revalidate, actual hand interaction can close the leaf, and a currently seen cuffed occupant can be escorted to an actual holding bay and stopped before resuming. Inaccessible coverage is never counted complete.",
    "Door opening aims at the leaf and checks both the shared displayed context and actual physical interaction query, preventing a short-fan casing selection from pulsing indefinitely. Door retreat uses the controller deterministic heading and scales clearance with leaf width.",
    "Protocol/replay v34 replicates active/queued room identity, route step, subtask and blocked state with scalar and atomic map-aware rejection. Private planning is reconstructed by ordinary input replay.",
    "The squad menu distinguishes searching, blocked, moving an occupant, securing a target and route searched. Route completion makes no all-clear or hidden-occupant claim."
  ],
